blocking_evidence:
  Three committed Red-test contradictions with spec AC2 make a passing Green gate impossible for any AC2-correct wrapper.
  1. tests/sound-set-mp3.test.ts, writeFakeFfmpeg: the fake derives its output path from args.indexOf('-o'). AC2 pins the ffmpeg argv with the output as the last positional argument and no -o. Probe of the committed fake with the exact AC2 argv: exit 0, no .mp3 written, ffmpeg-calls.log records the argv. Therefore case 1 cannot create the four fake files, the ffmpeg-fail-at branch cannot exit 3, and ffmpeg-no-write makes the fake writeFileSync('') and crash (exit 187 instead of the required 'wrote no file' line).
  2. tests/sound-set.test.ts and tests/sound-set.adversarial.test.ts: their run() helpers set EARSHOT_BIN only. The fake earshot writes the four bytes 'OggS' (or zero bytes). AC2 requires the MP3 step, and /usr/bin/ffmpeg is on PATH here, so the real binary rejects the fake input and the wrapper fails. Green output: "sound-set: ffmpeg failed for alpha (tap/soft) with exit 187" where the tests expect status 0 and no stderr. Red updated only case 1's stdout assertion; it did not give these fixtures a fake ffmpeg or the two .mp3 success lines.
  3. tests/sound-set.adversarial.test.ts: this file was not updated for the MP3 step. Its success cases assert stdout with no .mp3 lines. The case "stops at a later preparation failure and retains only earlier successful output" expects beta's ogg preparation error before alpha's ffmpeg step. AC2 requires per-entry order: prepare the two targets, render the Ogg, render the MP3. The case therefore contradicts AC2.
  Green failure list (17): 4 in sound-set-mp3.test.ts, 11 in sound-set.adversarial.test.ts, 2 in sound-set.test.ts.
  Full probe output: /home/daniebo/.cache/opencode/green-p2-probe.log.

handoff: Mid Red retry required for Phase 2. Do not edit the committed Red tests in Green. Keep AC2 unchanged and fix the three committed fixtures in a new Red commit, then rerun Red and Green. Required fixes: (A) tests/sound-set-mp3.test.ts writeFakeFfmpeg must take the output path from args[args.length - 1] so the pinned argv works and the fail-at and no-write branches trigger; (B) tests/sound-set.test.ts run() must set FFMPEG_BIN to a fake ffmpeg that writes a .mp3 from the last positional argv element, and case 1 must keep the two .mp3 success lines; (C) tests/sound-set.adversarial.test.ts success fixtures must set the same fake ffmpeg, assert stdout with the .mp3 line, and update the 'stops at a later preparation failure' expectation to AC2's per-entry order. The AC2 implementation already sits uncommitted in scripts/sound-set.mjs for the next Green run to verify and commit. No product decision was needed, so no question with options is put to the user.
